(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ce-easy-2026-002"]={"v":1,"id":"ce-easy-2026-002","title":"Advance Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","sourceTitle":"Advance Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","branch":"CIVIL ENGINEERING","code":"CE","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering","seriesId":"ce-easy-2026","num":2,"category":"advance","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering"},"source":"CIVIL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering/002_Advance Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>What is the value of the following expression?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/43/436737c36100a8d5650e.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/775815f36c5b93c9de4f.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c50c1196422ee583228.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bcf1e09681b6427fc176.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/59dd3055cfcf5696b1fe.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74a6e238e594a509ba24.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A student took five papers in an examination, where the full marks were the same for each paper. His marks in these papers were in the proportion of 6 : 7 : 8 : 9 : 10. In all papers together, the candidate obtained 60% of the total marks. Then the number of papers in which he got more than 50% marks is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"3"},{"key":"C","html":"4"},{"key":"D","html":"5"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1d528eeb164a6e990d6a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p><em>R</em>, <em>S</em> and <em>H</em> enter into a partnership and their capitals are in the proportion of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3410e67a2b48cb45032d.png\" /> <em>R</em> withdraws half his capital at the end of 4 months. Out of total annual profit of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae6b9218502367c98161.png\" /> <em>R</em>’s share is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d38e0c4d792cbdaaa8f.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4a/4a9adc4b7c36f4e079f2.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/668dbdf8a91ec7da4bd2.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/4259526ccd3a7fe25ee4.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea375a202e3afcb07691.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For this question, you have to base your conclusion on the three premises (viz: 1, 2 and 3). Assuming the facts in the statements to be true, which of the following conclusions logically follows from the statements?<br />\n<strong>Statements:</strong><br />\n1. Some cakes are bikes<br />\n2. Some bikes are hills<br />\n3. All laptops are bikes<br />\n<strong>Conclusions:</strong><br />\nI. All laptops are hills<br />\nII. Some laptops are cakes<br />\nIII. Some cakes are hills<br />\nIV. Some laptops are not cakes</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Only I follows"},{"key":"B","html":"Only either II or IV follows"},{"key":"C","html":"Only I or II follows"},{"key":"D","html":"Only I and IV follows"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/be9bff9429bd5d0aed43.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A messenger was returning to his base station which was in front of him to the north. When this base station was 100 m away from him, he turned to the left and moved 50 m to deliver the last message to the Peshwa’s troops. He then moved in the same direction for 40 m, turned to his<br />\nright and moved 100 m. How many meters away he is now from his base station?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"150"},{"key":"C","html":"90"},{"key":"D","html":"100"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e7b20176c1c05550a5e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A person starts typing the numbers from 1 to 1999. He press the keys total ‘n’ number of times.<br />\nThe value of <em>n</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6889"},{"key":"B","html":"1000"},{"key":"C","html":"2888"},{"key":"D","html":"none of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nThe number of times he pressed the keys for one digit number = 9<br />\nThe number of times he pressed the keys for two digit numbers = 90 &times; 2 = 180<br />\nThe numbers of times he pressed the keys for three digit numbers = 900 &times; 3 = 2700<br />\nThe number of times he pressed the keys for the numbers 1000 to 1999 is 1000 &times; 4 = 4000<br />\nThus, total number of times the keys are pressed = 6889</p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Choose the most appropriate word from the options given below to complete the following sentence.<br />\nBased on his recent poor decisions, it was obvious that Seth lacked even a _____ of good sense.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"debasement"},{"key":"B","html":"diversion"},{"key":"C","html":"disapprobation"},{"key":"D","html":"modicum"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nModicum is a small or token amount. It effectively conveys that Seth lacked even a small amount of good sense.</p>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Below is a sentence of which some parts have been jumbled up. Rearrange these parts which are labelled <em>P</em>, <em>Q</em>, <em>R</em> and <em>S</em> to produce the correct sentence. Choose the proper sequence. It would<br />\nP : that they were quite in the dark<br />\nQ : about the policy of management<br />\nR : appear from their statement<br />\nS : in dealing with the strike<br />\nThe proper sequence should be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"S R P Q"},{"key":"B","html":"R P Q S"},{"key":"C","html":"S Q R P"},{"key":"D","html":"R S Q P"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&ldquo;It would appear ...&rdquo; can be the only coherent beginning of the sentence. Thus the first part<br />\nwould be <em>R</em>. Since R says &ldquo;their statement&rdquo;, sentence P would follow it because it also says, &ldquo;that they ...&rdquo;<br />\nThus, option (b) is the correct answer.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>If you are a brisk walker, there is no need to go to a gym. Your neighbourhood can become your gym. You don’t need fancy equipment to get a good exercise either. All you need is a welldesigned pair of shoes.<br />\nThe paragraph best supports the statement that</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"poorly designed shoes can cause major foot injuries."},{"key":"B","html":"walking outdoors provides a better workout than walking indoors."},{"key":"C","html":"a gym membership is a poor investment."},{"key":"D","html":"brisk walking is a convenient and valuable form of exercise"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D, C, B, A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nBy stating that brisk walking does not require commute to a gym, the author stresses the<br />\nconvenience of this form of exercise. The paragraph also states that brisk walking may result in a good workout.<br />\nOption (c) is not appropriate. A gym membership can be a good investment for some.<br />\nOption (b) is not given in the passage.<br />\nOption (a) seems logical but the paragraph does not mention it.<br />\nOption (d) is the most appropriate option.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>How many triangles are there in the following figure?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aaf7f592fbedede41d37.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6"},{"key":"B","html":"10"},{"key":"C","html":"11"},{"key":"D","html":"12"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74beba64b6ff2d8dac2e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following statement(s) are incorrect for high strength bolt?<br />\n1. The tension in bolt is not uniform.<br />\n2. The frictional resistance is effective outside the hole.<br />\n3. There is no stress concentration in the bolt holes.<br />\n4. HSFG bolts provide flexible connection.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2 and 3"},{"key":"B","html":"1, 2 and 3"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3"},{"key":"D","html":"1 and 4"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; HSFG bolts provide rigid connection.<br />\n&bull; The tension in bolt is uniform.</p>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The magnitude of axial force in the member <em>AC</em> of frame as shown below is _____.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/632d7985af914164c4c2.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"75 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"37.5 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"56.5 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"93.5 kN"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c5/c5e7ff1de78cbc919855.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85daa7719d7a20ba3caf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following is not an effect of fly ash on cement concrete?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"It improves the resistance of concrete to sulphate attack."},{"key":"B","html":"It reduces the heat of hydration in concrete."},{"key":"C","html":"It increases the permeability of concrete."},{"key":"D","html":"It slows the rate of gain of strength in early days."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe permeability of concrete reduces on addition of fly ash to cement. 28 days permeability of<br />\nfly-ash-concrete may be three times as that of ordinary concrete but after 6 months it may be less<br />\nthan 0.25 times. So, it reduces the overall permeability of concrete.</p>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a circular arc section as shown in figure below. If S is the shear center of section, then the value of <em>x</em>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/65c09aa6ce67456d0bb6.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"127.324 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"77.324 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"27.324 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"32.245 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b1f63f5de834b57c8d0a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A prestressed concrete beam of span 8 m has width 300 mm and depth 600 mm. The initial stress in the tendons located at a constant eccentricity of 75 mm is 1500 N/mm<sup>2</sup>. The sectional area of the tendons is 120 mm<sup>2</sup>. The increase in stress in the wires when the beam supports a total dead of 10 kN/m including its self weight is ______ MPa. (Round off to nearest integer). (Take <em>E<sub>s</sub></em> = 210 kN/mm<sup>2</sup> and <em>E<sub>c</sub></em> = 30 kN/mm<sup>2</sup> and neglect the effect of axial force).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3],"answerText":"3","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3(3 - 3)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5ae98af1c1f745d468b1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A semicircular gate of radius 1.5 m and weighing 15 kN can swing freely about its horizontal diameter as shown in figure below. The gate is placed in such a way that it makes an angle of 40° with the free water surface. The water level on one side extends up to 6 m above the hinge<br />\n(diameter) of the gate. The minimum horizontal force required to keep the gate closed under the given conditions is _______ kN. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/32d183076edcb8545f9e.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[94.8,95.5],"answerText":"95.14","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>95.14(94.80 - 95.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ce/ce586430f2fcd46fb06e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/471961f3334188b48b4c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A wastewater treatment plant discharges its treated effluent into a nearby surface stream. The key characteristics of both the stream and the effluent are provided below. Assuming instantaneous and complete mixing of the effluent with the stream, select the incorrect statement(s) from the given options.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06f65b128ccfcabab10f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Assume saturation oxygen level of stream as 9.2 mg/<em>l</em>.</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Ultimate BOD of wastewater is 20.81 mg/l"},{"key":"B","html":"Ultimate BOD of wastewater is 194.86 mg/l"},{"key":"C","html":"Critical time of deficit concentration is 7.205 days"},{"key":"D","html":"Critical time of DO deficit is 3.276 days"}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e07a6d94898cd4ef1c0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the distance-time graph as shown in the figure. A slow moving vehicle with speed u<em><sub>B </sub></em>(whose distance-time plot is shown as a dotted line) enters a traffic stream originally moving at speed uA, density <em>k<sub>A</sub></em> and flow <em>q<sub>A</sub></em>. Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct in reference to the graph shown?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/654355297c93e962bdac.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Two shock waves are formed in the given situation."},{"key":"B","html":"Line <em>AB</em> represents platoon dissipating shock wave."},{"key":"C","html":"Line <em>BC</em> represents platoon forming shock wave."},{"key":"D","html":"The slow moving vehicle leaves the traffic stream at point <em>Q</em>."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e215eb2328f612268b6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The loading period for a building is from June 2000 to June 2002. In June 2005, the average measured settlement was found to be 100 mm. It is known that the ultimate settlement will be about 250 mm. The settlement in June 2025 is _______ mm. (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[218,219],"answerText":"218.45","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>218.45(218 - 219)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e7aaca1d9411f12162a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The critical duration for a maintenance project having details as shown in table below is _____ days. (Round off to nearest integer).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/9131b7be0d6bcbbcd5b7.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[42,42],"answerText":"42","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>42 (42 - 42)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e1291bbe2ed5ba40fc93.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>If <em>A</em> is a 3 × 3 real matrix with eigen values 1, 2 and 3, then the matrix <em>A</em> satisfies</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9f8daf14dd18ee97cade.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/75668bd410c4e06ed846.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d71693efde787dba3f0a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22ee2d5705ea0f603718.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/61/6100934e925cb8217582.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/30cdfb08e3d3e52d617c.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"log(2)"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3b2a8eafbe0fcd924fff.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/1149bd19a21716f0cf62.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/60124ce6f83d52ba8359.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/dade9faaf92b07779ca4.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Flue gas emission occurs through a vertical stack. The physical height of the stack is 210 m with an internal diameter of 1.1 m. The ambient wind speed is 3.8 m/s, the air temperature is 15°C and the barometric pressure is 1000 millibars. The stack gas velocity is 9.5 m/s and its temperature is 152°C. Assuming neutral atmospheric conditions, the effective height of the stack is ______ m.<br />\n(Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[216.55,216.95],"answerText":"216.74","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>216.74(216.55 - 216.95)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a172c6d6fa5b4c789526.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A rectangular area of 4 m × 8 m carries a uniform load of 120 kN/m<sup>2</sup> at the ground surface.<br />\nVertical pressure at 10 m below the centre and corner of loaded area are _______.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/07/07eba38817bcef8756d4.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"15.74 kN/m<sup>2</sup> and 3.936 kN/m<sup>2</sup> respectively"},{"key":"B","html":"4.416 kN/m<sup>2</sup> and 3.936 kN/m<sup>2</sup> respectively"},{"key":"C","html":"15.74 kN/m<sup>2</sup> and 11.17 kN/m<sup>2</sup> respectively"},{"key":"D","html":"11.17 kN/m<sup>2</sup> and 4.416 kN/m<sup>2</sup> respectively"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9de13627f9829464ad20.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/07/071e32e827c26452b63b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In spot speed study, total 1200 vehicles were observed. If upper and lower safe limit from cumulative percentage frequency distribution curve were found as 45 km/hr and 15 km/hr respectively, then the total number of vehicles moving between 15 km/hr to 45 km/hr would be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1020 vehicles"},{"key":"B","html":"840 vehicles"},{"key":"C","html":"996 vehicles"},{"key":"D","html":"1050 vehicles"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/dbc64b7b27924be72213.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The effective stress shear strength parameters of a completely saturated clay are <em>C</em>′ = 15 kN/m<sup>2 </sup>and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/0981aae473009b05f403.png\" /> = 20°. A sample of this clay was tested in a UU test under a cell pressure of 250 kN/m<sup>2</sup> and the principal stress difference at failure was 100 kN/m2. The value of pore water pressure at failure was:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"135.7 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"195.03 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"212.56 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"178.76 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/6349573a196d21eee18f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A smooth flat plate of 1.5 m width and 4 m length moves through an oil of relative density 0.85 at a speed of 2 m/s along its length. The thickness of the boundary layer at the center is _____ cm. (Take ν = 8 × 10<sup>–5</sup> m<sup>3</sup>/s, answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4.4,4.6],"answerText":"4.47","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.47(4.40 - 4.60)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/991e746fcfb175ca3236.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A rectangular channel of width 3.5 m has a bed slope of 0.00018. The Manning’s roughness coefficient (n) for the channel is 0.020. The channel carries a discharge of 0.90 m<sup>3</sup>/s. Assuming that the hydraulic radius is equal to the flow depth, the slope of the water surface with respect to the horizontal at a section where the depth of flow is 0.70 m is ________ × 10<sup>–4</sup>. (Answer upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-0.86,-0.83],"answerText":"-0.849","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-0.849(-0.860 - -0.830)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ee/ee4dee4844a3d92ebc2b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In remote sensing, which of the following correctly matches the type of resolution with the aspect it defines in an image?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Spatial resolution – Ability to distinguish between two closely spaced wavelength bands."},{"key":"B","html":"Spectral resolution – Refers to the sensitivity of the system to small changes in the wavelength"},{"key":"C","html":"Temporal resolution – Frequency of image acquisition over the same area"},{"key":"D","html":"Radiometric resolution – Sharpness or clarity of surface details in an image"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nSpatial resolution &ndash; Ability of the remote sensing system to record spatial details.<br />\nSpectral resolution &ndash; Wavelength to which the remote sensing system is sensitive.<br />\nRadiometric resolution &ndash; Sensitivity of the system to small changes in the radiation (wavelength).</p>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For a dam resting on anisotropic soil, a flow net has been prepared using a vertical scale of 1 : 25. The length of the dam base as measured from the flow net drawing is 3 m, whereas the actual base width of the dam in the field is 100 m. The ratio of the permeability of the soil in the horizontal direction to that in the vertical direction is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.33"},{"key":"B","html":"0.75"},{"key":"C","html":"0.563"},{"key":"D","html":"1.78"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/eb/eb84a245811f67b7adb9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If the ruling gradient on a B.G. track is 1 in 250 and a 5 degree curve is provided on the track and actual ruling gradient is expressed as 1 in n, then the value of n is ________. (Round off to nearest integer)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[500,500],"answerText":"500","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>500(500 - 500)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/393513bd7866d81460c9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A sample of biodegradable municipal solid waste (MSW) has the empirical formula C<sub>90</sub>H<sub>230</sub>O<sub>50</sub> N. It is completely aerobically stabilized. The oxygen content in air is 23% by weight and the density of air can be assumed as 1.25 kg/m<sup>3</sup>. Atomic masses are : C-12, H-1, O-16, N-14. If 2 tons of this waste undergoes complete oxidative degradation then the theoretical volume of air required is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2783.6 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"3841.2 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"12598.4 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"6299.3 m<sup>3</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/adbf44e08d5ab900c4c0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statement(s) is/are incorrect ?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"An element in plane stress can never be in state of plane strain."},{"key":"B","html":"An element in plane stress is always in state of plane strain."},{"key":"C","html":"If an element is in state of triaxial stress, then stresses acting on element are principal stresses."},{"key":"D","html":"Planes of maximum shear strains are inclined at 45° to direction of principle strains."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)<br />\nAn element in plane stress can&rsquo;t be in state of plane strain except when Poisson&rsquo;s ratio is zero or<br />\nwhen normal stresses acting on element are equal and opposite.</p>"},{"n":34,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A horizontal venturimeter with an inlet diameter of 140 mm and throat diameter of 70 mm is used to measure the flow of water. The discharge coefficient of the venturimeter is 0.97. The inlet pressure is 15 kPa (gauge), the atmospheric pressure is 98.5 kPa (absolute) and the vapor pressure of water is 3.2 kPa (absolute). The maximum discharge that can pass through the venturimeter without cavitation is _________ <em>l</em>/s. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[57,57.5],"answerText":"57.26","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>57.26(57.00 - 57.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/1488b63d0f3960f6274c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3cfd5a94791498617f6e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The angle between the tangents to the curve <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8b6e30eeca6798155862.png\" /> at the point <em>t</em> = ±1 is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/299bdb96bc2e7dfb0446.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/37e5885751d81d70b626.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c07a3e3ad0a06bfa1de1.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d892502e51606ff692b4.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/23cfb6ab7e75f50e1892.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A wastewater sample contains 90 mg/l methanol (CH<sub>3</sub>OH) and 130 mg/l acetic acid (CH<sub>3</sub>COOH).<br />\nThe ratio <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/acd106639294faef7d36.png\" /> (total organic carbon to chemical oxygen demand.) for acetic acid is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.667"},{"key":"B","html":"0.375"},{"key":"C","html":"0.333"},{"key":"D","html":"0.2997"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19386f10ac034bfa7db7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1be55711f25613fe8a33.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Natural frequency for the structural system shown in figure below is ______ rad/sec (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<p>(Take, <em>EI</em> = 2 × 10<sup>6</sup> N-m<sup>2</sup> and g = 9.81 m/s<sup>2</sup>).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/78b1fcc53c3e1f27cb07.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.68,2.74],"answerText":"2.71","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.71(2.68 - 2.74)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2cb465295834e8914748.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":38,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A short circular column of diameter 500 mm is to be helically reinforced and its ultimate load carrying capacity is to be 2500 kN. If M25 grade of concrete and Fe415 steel are to be used, then the area of compression reinforcement will be ______ mm2. (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1568,1572],"answerText":"1570.8","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1570.8(1568 - 1572)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/443295426d58e706ad31.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Match list-I (Type of valve) with list-II (Function/Description) and select the correct code given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5e7a14be07349f8a4a6.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A simply supported beam of span L carries a central load P. The sectional area of the beam is so designed that the moment of inertia of the section increases uniformly from <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/9830af0879a07af5bb3a.png\" /> at the ends to 1.51 in the middle as shown in figure. The central deflection of the beam will be</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b9609bee9a44224db3a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8ac56aebdb358dd785a0.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3b267d97e1c1190cb0ed.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b0c1275ca982bb1c9b0.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22ce05e0952bfc918c9e.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef5cc58bc2e1fadd6cc1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/982d9812fee11542f40e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A truss is shown in figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/aec3c62b5da2d312497b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The magnitude of force in member EF is _________ kN. (Answer upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[37.3,37.7],"answerText":"37.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>37.5(37.3 - 37.7)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9db1e212a7a0976e0677.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>During aerial photogrammetry, the mean photo base length between two successive photographs is 95 mm. The flying height above ground level at the time of exposure is 1800 m and the focal length of the camera lens is 210 mm. If the height of a building on the ground is 36 m, then the parallax difference between the top and bottom of the building is ______ mm. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.9,2],"answerText":"1.94","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.94(1.90 - 2.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/59363204799a64d53603.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The cross-section of a cutting in a homogeneous saturated clay soil is inclined at a slope of 2H : 1 V with height of 10 m. The factor of safety against immediate shear failure along the slip circle as shown in figure ignoring the tension crack will be:<br />\n[Take bulk unit weight of soil, γ<sub>b</sub> = 20 kN/m<sup>3</sup>, undrained unit cohesion, C<sub>u</sub> = 25 kN/m<sup>2</sup>].</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/23e455f7611947087756.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.32"},{"key":"B","html":"1.18"},{"key":"C","html":"1.54"},{"key":"D","html":"2.1"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f8127cffffa27b30f33.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The consistency and flow resistance of a sample of bitumen can be determinated through which of the following test?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Viscosity test"},{"key":"B","html":"Penetration test"},{"key":"C","html":"Ductility test"},{"key":"D","html":"Softening point test"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nViscosity is measure of a fluid&rsquo;s resistance to flow. This test determines how easily bitumen can flow under specific condition.</p>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A sample of clay from the clay layer 10 m thick as shown below in figure is tested in lab. The results of sample of clay shows decrement in void ratio from 0.7 to 0.55 by increasing stress from 150 kN/ m<sup>2</sup> to 300 kN/m<sup>2</sup>. The settlement of given clay layer under given circular footing will be:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ecb77f75a6a955d633cd.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>[Take stress distribution as 1.5H : 1 V, and γ<em><sub>w</sub></em> = 10 kN/m<sup>3</sup>.]</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"150.49 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"107.39 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"125.19 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"120.30 mm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/72/72fcb4a786e2886356cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two lagoons are connected in series and receive a discharge of 7200 m<sup>3</sup>/day. The influent entering the system contains 90 mg/l of biodegradable contaminant. At steady state, the effluent from the entire system must not exceed 25 mg/l. Assume that both lagoons are well mixed and have the<br />\nsame biodegradation rate constant.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0c4ada728cdb24471e80.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The biodegradation rate constant for the lagoons is ________ per day. (Answer upto three decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.08,0.09],"answerText":"0.083","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.083(0.080 - 0.090)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5d7dbbc7e20fcb9caa2d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The solution of the ordinary differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2a7ce1d066cf08524b51.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e3b3d3cfd45b4bed0a6.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/262ceef09dfcc0c47975.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bf/bff3e67d01085d8c0ca0.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd1ac00437add890eb69.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3c00ed67b5324bdd1304.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Three white and three black balls, kept in three bins are arranged in four ways as shown below. In each arrangement, a bin has to be chosen randomly and only one ball needs to be picked randomly from the chosen bin. Which of the following arrangements has the probability for<br />\ngetting a white ball picked less than or equal to 0.5?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/96032ead404c29e5f23a.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/839510fda98e865bac0e.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/07/07670a6b8d2178e66512.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e8a30dcd3500e775808.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/443ef65c65cfadfc05cc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A wastewater treatment unit uses a long closed pipe as a plug flow reactor (PFR) for disinfection before discharge. The influent wastewater contains 4 × 105 fecal coliform colony forming units (CFU) per litre, while the permissible discharge limit is 2500 CFU/<em>l</em>. The decay of microorganisms follow first-order kinetics with a rate constant of 0.23 per min. The average flow velocity through the pipe is 1.2 m/s. Assuming steady-state plug flow and complete mixing in the cross-section only, the required length of the pipe for achieving the desired disinfection level is ______ m. (Answer upto one decimal place).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1588.5,1589],"answerText":"1588.8","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1588.8(1588.5 - 1589.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c6c65d01db9a343d8e3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two blocks P and Q weighing 1.2 kN and 2.5 kN respectively are in equilibrium as shown in the figure. The coefficient of friction between the two blocks as well as between block Q and the horizontal floor is 0.35. The minimum horizontal force ‘F’ required to just start moving block Q is _______ kN. (Answer upto three decimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/dfb9dde8754cd9745f31.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.56,1.59],"answerText":"1.574","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.574 (1.560 - 1.590)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab166322772695038f64.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c709f826cc8f3bac1b0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A rectangular footing of size 1.5 m × 3.0 m is placed at a depth of 2.5 m below the ground surface in a saturated clay having a unit weight of 19 kN/m<sup>3</sup> and an unconfined compressive strength of 120 kN/m<sup>2</sup>. Assuming a factor of safety of 3.0, determine the safe bearing capacity of the soil<br />\nusing Skempton’s analysis.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"178.3 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"167.5 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"194.1 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"120.8 kN/m<sup>2</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa8f8d75647f6f873ade.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A regular pentagon PQRST is drawn an a map. If the backbearing of side <em>PQ</em> is 216°, then fore bearing of the line RS is ________ degree. (Round off to nearest integer).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[180,180],"answerText":"180","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>180(180 - 180)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9d2d79454b86326491d1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A square flexible footing, 3.0 m on each side, carries a total load of 1500 kN and rests on a cohesive soil. The soil has a modulus of elasticity of 10 MPa and Poisson’s ratio of 0.38. Assuming an influence factor of 0.7, the elastic settlement at the center of the footing is _______ mm. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[29.9,30],"answerText":"29.95","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>29.95(29.90 - 30.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/1510ac686bbdca79cdb2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Three identical walls, each 12 cm in diameter, are located at the vertices of an equilateral triangle with a spacing of 15 m between them. The wells fully penetrate a confined aquifer of thickness 18 m. The coefficient of permeability of the aquifer is 25 m/day and the radius of influence of each well is 500 m. When pumped simultaneously under steady conditions, the drawdown in each well is observed to be 2.5 m. The percentage reduction in discharge per well due to interference is approximately:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"43.72%"},{"key":"B","html":"77.68%"},{"key":"C","html":"25.46%"},{"key":"D","html":"62.67%"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26e067d399afd62e4242.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A two lane highway has a horizontal curve of radius 280 m and total length of curve is 300 m. The distance between centerline of highway and centerline of inner lane is 1.90 m. The setback distance from inner edge of road is:<br />\n[Take sight distance as 350 m]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"48.53 m"},{"key":"B","html":"49.20 m"},{"key":"C","html":"50.41 m"},{"key":"D","html":"52.45 m"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f019cc2890f1cb6cfaf1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The effective length factor (k) of a prismatic compression member whose one end is restrained against translation and rotation both whereas the other end is restrained against rotation but not restrained against translation is ______. (Answer upto one decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.2,1.2],"answerText":"1.2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.2(1.2 - 1.2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/156577ddfdf467c041a0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A pile of 40 cm diameter and 4 m long, is driven in a uniform clay of unconfined compressive strength 80 kN/m<sup>2</sup>. The safe frictional resistance of the pile will be<br />\n[Take, adhesion factor (α) and factor of safety (FOS) as 0.6 and 2 respectively].</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"120.63 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"180.93 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"60.32 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"241.26 kN"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/38/38c89d5a187d443f6dba.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A hydraulic jump occurs in a horizontal rectangular channel, where the ratio of sequent depths is 11.25. The energy dissipated during the jump with respect to the initial specific energy of flow is _______. (Answer upto one decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[67,68],"answerText":"67.5","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>67.5(67 - 68)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0a/0a9524817fbe1bf59cab.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Flood data for a river covering the period 1990 to 2020 shows that the mean annual flood discharge is 27,200 m<sup>3</sup>/s with a standard deviation of 13,240 m<sup>3</sup>/s. For a proposed bridge at this site, it is desired to have an acceptable risk of 10% during its design life of 40 years. The design flood<br />\ndischarge for this return period is estimated using Gumbel’s method. If the actual discharge adopted for design is 1,00,000 m<sup>3</sup>/s, then the safety margin with respect to the maximum expected flood discharge is ________ m<sup>3</sup>/s. (Rounded off to nearest integer, take <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb6bdd591c4985e45238.png\" /> = 0.5380 and <em>S<sub>n</sub></em> = 1.1193)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8895,8915],"answerText":"8904","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8904(8895 - 8915)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f2fb4a95c8a6688bbe6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A fixed beam of span ‘2<em>l</em> ’ carries uniformly distributed load ‘w’ over half of the span as shown in figure below.</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bd/bdb0a523bf650e2bbf51.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The collapse load for the beam is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a8a6629361821cf7da3.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a4884d078c4971ef9f4.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/97b2c9de029a3c679c76.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/ad229eea8613fd397a04.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8efb75de2bc42b2b05ce.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A concrete gravity dam has a base width of 80 m. The total resisting moment and overturning moment about the toe are 4125.480 MN-m and 2789.360 MN-m respectively. The total vertical (downward) load acting on the dam base is 65 MN. The ratio of magnitude of the normal stress<br />\ndeveloped at the heel to the normal stress developed at the toe of the dam base is _________.<br />\n(Answer upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.186,0.186],"answerText":"0.186","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.186(0.160 - &ndash; 0.200)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e663c7be1fda1d6652ac.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A baseline was measured six times and the following lengths (in meters) were recorded : 24.632, 24.628, 24.635, 24.642, 24.633 and 24.625. Assuming all observations are equally reliable, which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Probable error in single observation is ± 3.973 × 10<sup>–3</sup>."},{"key":"B","html":"Probable error in most probable value is ± 1.62 × 10<sup>–3</sup>."},{"key":"C","html":"Probable error in most probable value is ± 8.723 × 10<sup>–6</sup>."},{"key":"D","html":"Probable value is 24.6325 ± 0.00005234."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/196965a367bbf15f2e5c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If α<em>x</em> + βy + 9 ln |2<em>x</em> + 3y – γ| = <em>x</em> + <em>c</em> is the solution of (2<em>x </em>+ 3y – 2)<em>dx</em> + (4<em>x</em> + 6y – 7)dy = 0, then α + β + γ = _______.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[18,18],"answerText":"18","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>18 (18 - 18)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/197565c1882b8402d9ef.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Let a die be rolled till 2 is obtained. The probability that 2 is obtained on even numbered toss is equal to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/320682e4a6958f35ad47.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a2/a25df71bde9a794b6e0c.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8fe9e1c9973d0478c4ae.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d564dec697ec4f6643c1.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/eab0284b59fb215d00ad.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/68af7de2eff291900c56.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"-1"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"0"},{"key":"D","html":"2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d2e0196f5d6f7c50017.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":37,"MSQ":5,"NAT":23},"withoutKey":0}};
